notes.body:
**Current merge request: **

```
tp_offset = (tvb_get_ntohl(tvb, offset) & SOMEIP_TP_OFFSET_MASK);
proto_tree_add_uint(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_offset, tvb, offset, 4, tp_offset);
proto_tree_add_item(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_reserved, tvb, offset, 4, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);
proto_tree_add_item_ret_boolean(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_more_segments, tvb, offset, 4, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN, &tp_more_segments);
offset += 4;
```

```
    SOME/IP-TP: 000005716c6d6e6f707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f808182838485868788898a8b…
        Offset: 1392
        .... .... .... .... .... .... .... 000. = Reserved: 0x0
        .... .... .... .... .... .... .... ...1 = More Segments: True
        Payload: 6c6d6e6f707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f808182838485868788898a8b8c8d8e8f…
```
Offset is set correctly as filter: OK.


What I do I want but it seems it is not possible to limitation of the API:
```
    SOME/IP-TP: 000005716c6d6e6f707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f808182838485868788898a8b…
        0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0101 0111 .... = Offset:  1392
        .... .... .... .... .... .... .... 000. = Reserved: 0x0
        .... .... .... .... .... .... .... ...1 = More Segments: True
        Payload: 6c6d6e6f707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f808182838485868788898a8b8c8d8e8f…
```
Offset is set correctly as filter: OK.


**Option 2: Same code but bitmask set**

**Option 3: proto_tree_add_bits_ret_val**

**Option 4: proto_tree_add_item and mask set**
```
        0000 0000  0000 0000  0000 0101  0111 .... = Offset: 87
```
Offset is set correctly as filter: **NOT OK!**

**Option 5, ...**
`proto_tree_add_bitmask_list_ret_uint64`, `proto_item_add_bitmask_tree`, ... have all the same issue.

They end up calling `proto_tree_add_uint`, which calls `proto_tree_set_uint` and the problem is:
```
	if (hfinfo->bitmask) {
		/* Mask out irrelevant portions */
		integer &= (guint32)(hfinfo->bitmask);

		/* Shift bits */
		integer >>= hfinfo_bitshift(hfinfo);

		FI_SET_FLAG(fi, FI_BITS_OFFSET(hfinfo_bitoffset(hfinfo)));
		FI_SET_FLAG(fi, FI_BITS_SIZE(hfinfo_mask_bitwidth(hfinfo)));
	}
```

If bitmask is set, you CANNOT set the value directly with the current API. :disappointed: 


The only other alternative to the merge request could be something like this:
```
        proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_offset_encoded, tvb, offset, 4, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN, &tp_offset);
        tp_offset <<= 4;
        proto_tree_add_item(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_reserved, tvb, offset, 4, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);
        proto_tree_add_item_ret_boolean(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_more_segments, tvb, offset, 4, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN, &tp_more_segments);
        ti = proto_tree_add_uint(tp_tree, hf_someip_tp_offset, tvb, offset, 4, tp_offset);
        PROTO_ITEM_SET_GENERATED(ti);
        offset += 4;
```

```
    SOME/IP-TP: 000005716c6d6e6f707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f808182838485868788898a8b…
        0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0101 0111 .... = Encoded Offset: 0x0000057
        .... .... .... .... .... .... .... 000. = Reserved: 0x0
        .... .... .... .... .... .... .... ...1 = More Segments: True
        [Offset: 1392]
        Payload: 6c6d6e6f707172737475767778797a7b7c7d7e7f808182838485868788898a8b8c8d8e8f…

```

It seems that `proto_tree_add_uint_bits_format_value` uses:

`decode_bits_in_field` and this adds 2 spaces between bytes:
```
        if (bit && !(bit % 4)) {
            str[str_p] = ' ';
            str_p++;
        }
        if (bit && !(bit % 8)) {
            str[str_p] = ' ';
            str_p++;
        }
```

Not sure what the others are using but only one space between bytes.

